---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Who We Are"
  description="Eshkere is an early-stage exploratory organization concept built around one thesis: Maximize Health, Play Games."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About Us"
    title="Who We Are"
    lead="Eshkere is an early-stage exploratory organization concept. That sentence is doing honest work: there is a thesis, a name, a visual identity and this website — and not yet much more."
  />

  <article class="who section">
    <div class="container--narrow prose">
      <p>
        <strong>Eshkere is built around one idea: Maximize Health, Play Games.</strong> Health —
        physical, mental and social well-being — is the non-optional foundation of human
        flourishing. Games are everything people can choose to pursue on top of that foundation:
        enjoyment, achievement, identity, exploration, creativity, relationships, knowledge,
        meaning and play.
      </p>
      <p>
        What kind of organization that idea deserves is exactly what is being explored. Eshkere
        might become a company, a fund, a studio, a research group, a community — or some
        combination that doesn't have a clean name yet. The exploration is happening in public,
        which is why this site exists before the answers do.
      </p>

      <h2>What exists today</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The thesis, developed in <a href={url('/our-approach')}>Our Approach</a>.</li>
        <li>A visual identity and this website — built as a serious institutional prototype.</li>
        <li>
          A commitment to honesty about stage: no invented staff, partners, funding, portfolio or
          history anywhere on this site.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What does not exist yet</h2>
      <p>
        A team roster, a funded portfolio, formal partnerships, offices, a publication record.
        Where those things would appear, you will find deliberate empty states instead — each one a
        placeholder for something real, not a performance of maturity.
      </p>

      <h2>Why the name sounds like that</h2>
      <p>
        “Eshkere” carries the energy of the games layer — an exclamation, a let's-go. The visual
        language of the brand borrows from video games and hyperpop on purpose: play is allowed to
        look joyful. The seriousness lives underneath, in the health-first ordering the whole
        project stands on.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="container who__links">
      <a class="who__link panel" href={url('/about-us/history')}>
        <span class="eyebrow">Our History</span>
        <span>How the story is being documented</span>
      </a>
      <a class="who__link panel" href={url('/about-us/partner-with-us')}>
        <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--pink">Partner With Us</span>
        <span>Shape what Eshkere becomes</span>
      </a>
      <a class="who__link panel" href={url('/about-us/team')}>
        <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--lime">Team</span>
        <span>Who is behind this (so far)</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .who {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4rem;
  }

  .who__links {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .who__link {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 1.6rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    transition: transform var(--speed-quick) var(--ease-out),
      border-color var(--speed-quick) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .who__link:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    border-color: var(--line-strong);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
